  ETH/SOL and multiple feature cards still render literal placeholder content (`— PLACEHOLDER —`, `PLACEHOLDER — NEEDS WIRING`) as if they were UI values, which violates the task requirement that unresolved sections be explicitly marked with `MISSING_EVIDENCE`/`BLOCKED` plus source pointers. This can mislead operators into thinking these are current display values instead of explicit evidence gaps.

- [P2] Replace fabricated risk config defaults with runtime values — /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT REBUILD/v2/frontend/src/pages/positions/index.tsx:188-189
  The risk-config panel inserts `'canary default'` and `'profile default'` when `confidence_gate_threshold` / `max_position_size_usdt` are missing, but these are not guaranteed to be present in the task’s current risk payload. Showing guessed defaults masks missing-evidence and can present non-existent settings as if they are the actual runtime config.

